<title>FRANCE: French Treasury to hold May OAT, Ecu sales early.</title>
<headline>French Treasury to hold May OAT, Ecu sales early.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury said on Monday its regular auctions of French franc OATs and Ecu bonds in May would both be held a day early because of public holidays in France.</p>
<p>The OAT auction, normally held on the first Thursday of each month, will be on Wednesday, April 30. The Ecu auction, normally held on the second Thursday of each month, will be on Wednesday, May 7, the Treasury said in a statement.</p>
<p>The second round of non-competitive bids will be held as usual on the Friday following each auction.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
